{"type":"message","id":"48af8dd0","parentId":"6ad30b58","timestamp":"2026-05-17T16:02:49.458Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The server is returning 500 Internal Server Error with \"error code: 1101\". This is a Cloudflare Workers error. The 1101 error is \"Worker threw exception\" - there's a runtime error in the Worker script. This isn't a client error - it's a server-side issue.\n\nThe error \"error code: 1101\" with a 500 response means the Workers runtime threw an exception. This is likely a bug in the Cloudflare Worker code itself, not an issue with my request.\n\nHowever, the GET requests work fine. The issue might be with the `/send` endpoint specifically, or with the content of my message.\n\nLet me try to GET /send or check if there's another endpoint. Actually wait, the 500 error body is literally just \"error code: 1101\" - this looks like it's the Workers runtime error format.\n\n\nSince my GET requests succeeded but the POST failed, the problem is likely in how I'm formatting the send request. I should experiment with simpler payloads and different content types, or maybe I'm using an HTTP method that the endpoint doesn't support. Let me look at the API documentation more carefully to see if there's a different endpoint or method I should be calling instead.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-ce7ba026-ac64-479d-a8c2-2787632f2596","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/\" 2>&1 | head -20\ncurl -s \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/health\" 2>&1 | head -20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":2296,"output":320,"cacheRead":17936,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":20552,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779033755167,"responseId":"chatcmpl-eb